INT. THE DAILY CHRONICLE - COMPOSING ROOM - NIGHT - 1888

Gaslight. Cases of type. Ink-black walls. A press thumps below.

ALDOUS FENWICK, 50s, foreman, rolls his sleeves. BRIDIE QUINN, 20s, compositor, sets type with quick fingers. TOMASZ KRAWCZYK, 30s, pressman, hauls a forme. PERPETUA LISLE, 40s, proofreader, spectacles on a ribbon, scowls at a galley. CYRIL BEAMISH, 17, devil, sweeps.

A brass speaking tube on the wall WHISTLES. Everyone freezes.

ALDOUS
(to the tube)
Composing room.

LORD HASTWELL (V.O.)
(muffled, imperious)
Fenwick. The front page.

ALDOUS
Set and locked, my lord.

LORD HASTWELL (V.O.)
Pull it. A fire in Whitechapel. Use my headline.

BRIDIE
(under her breath)
There's no room.

ALDOUS
Hush, girl.

LORD HASTWELL (V.O.)
Was that a woman?

ALDOUS
A compositor, sir.

LORD HASTWELL (V.O.)
Dismiss her.

Silence. Bridie's hand closes over her composing stick. Tomasz steps toward the tube.

TOMASZ
Dismiss me too.

PERPETUA
And me.

CYRIL
(squeaking)
And me.

Aldous pushes the cover onto the tube. The whistle dies. He turns slowly to face the room, and a smile breaks across his face.

ALDOUS
Gentlemen. Ladies. Set the page.
